# Where egres stands on each record of the .pgout beside this file:
# <tag>	<source>	<first line>	<note>, in record order.
#   skip      not supported yet; note = egres's error. Written by
#             run.py --write-skips, which keeps every other line.
#   bug       diverges, filed; note = the issue.
#   accepted  diverges on purpose; note = the reason.
# Known decisions: numeric keeps 38 digits (i128), results past 38
# digits round, and literals past numeric's range become float8.
# Today they surface only as unsupported numeric(210,10) DDL (see
# skips), so none of those appear here.
